* ============================================================
*  PINOCCHIO RELATIONAL -- READ-ONLY SHAKEDOWN (Phase 3a, AIF-167)
*
*  Status:  CANDIDATE / REVIEW_BEFORE_EXECUTION. READ-ONLY (no mutation).
*  Purpose: First runtime shakedown of the RELATIONAL surface at scale:
*           REL declarations + ENUM/JOIN emission, SQLsel joins, aggregates,
*           subqueries and set operations, over STUDENTS (1,000,000) and
*           ENROLL (5,501,358) -- the parent/child pair the fixtures were
*           built for and no Phase 1 battery ever joined.
*
*  THE CROSS-ORACLE IDENTITIES (the point of this battery)
*  -------------------------------------------------------
*  Two independent relational implementations walk the same data; their
*  counts must agree with each other AND with native scans. Parity between
*  two engines is not correctness (EVALDIFF lesson), so every identity below
*  is anchored to a THIRD, non-relational count:
*    I1  PHYSICAL counts: STUDENTS 1000000, ENROLL 5501358 (ORDER PHYSICAL --
*        under an active order, COUNT walks the tag, and a gutted tag lies)
*    I2  SQLsel INNER JOIN COUNT(*) ON SID == 5501358 (every child has a parent)
*    I3  canary triple agreement: REL LIST == REL ENUM rows == SQLsel
*        canary-join COUNT == 8 for SID 50000000 (REL is current-parent scoped)
*    I4  SQLsel LEFT JOIN COUNT(*)         == I2 + reported left-extended rows
*    I5  native COUNT FOR MAJOR = "CSCI"   == SQLsel COUNT(*) ALLTRIM(MAJOR)='CSCI'
*    I6  GROUP BY MAJOR row count          == DISTINCT MAJOR row count
*    I7  IN-subquery student count         == 1000000 - LEFT-unmatched parents
*    I8  UNION 150 / INTERSECT 50 / EXCEPT 50 on overlapping 100-row SID bands
*
*  SCANLIMIT HONESTY (g_scan_limit default 500000, set_relations.cpp:122):
*  the first REL LIST ALL runs AT the default against a 5.5M child and MUST
*  print the bounds warning ("BOUNDS, not totals"). That warning firing is a
*  PASS datum; silence there is a regression of the scan-limit honesty gate.
*
*  RUNTIME: multi-minute. The full-walk verbs (REL LIST at 12M budget, the
*  join counts, GROUP BY, the IN subquery) each pass 1M-5.5M rows. Each
*  ELAPSED (SET TIMER ON) is the datum -- do not abort early.
*
*  RUN (host, top-level runner so per-command SET TIMER fires):
*    powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\dottalkpp\data\scripts\pinocchio\run_pinocchio_relational_teed.ps1
* ============================================================
SET ECHO OFF
SET TIMER ON
SET TALK ON

SET PATH DBF DBF/pinocchio
SET PATH INDEXES INDEXES/pinocchio
SET PATH LMDB LMDB/pinocchio

ECHO === R0. open the pair: area 1 STUDENTS, area 2 ENROLL ===
* FIRST-RUN LESSON (2026-09-20, transcript relational_readonly_teed_20260920T160609Z):
* bare COUNT under an ACTIVE order walks the LOGICAL ROWSET -- i.e. the TAG --
* so a gutted index makes COUNT report the tag's cardinality (200 / 686 that
* day, LMDB envs deleted) and every identity downstream inherits the lie.
* Anchors are therefore taken with ORDER PHYSICAL, and R0c/R0d are the
* tag-sanity gates: bare COUNT under the ACTIVE TAG answers from the tag's
* own view, and that number MUST equal the physical COUNT beside it.
* 200-vs-1000000 there = gutted index; STOP, rebuild (BUILDLMDB HUGE CLEAN
* YES per table), rerun. Nothing in the engine checks this for you yet.
* GATE MECHANICS (corrected after watching the 2026-09-20 rerun): SET ORDER
* itself prints NO count. The probe is bare COUNT, whose answer depends on the
* order state -- ORDER PHYSICAL scans the file (~23 s / 1M, the truth), while
* an ACTIVE TAG answers from the tag's own view (O(1); the gutted tags said
* 200 / 686 there). So each gate is the PAIR: physical COUNT, then tag COUNT,
* and the two numbers MUST be equal. Cheap, decisive, and the second number
* is exactly the one that lied on the first run.
SELECT 1
USE STUDENTS
ECHO --- R0a. IDENTITY I1 anchor (parent): PHYSICAL count must be 1000000 ---
SET ORDER TO PHYSICAL
COUNT
ECHO --- R0c. tag-sanity gate: COUNT under TAG SID must equal R0a ---
SET ORDER TO TAG SID
COUNT
SELECT 2
USE ENROLL
ECHO --- R0b. IDENTITY I1 anchor (child): PHYSICAL count must be 5501358 ---
SET ORDER TO PHYSICAL
COUNT
ECHO --- R0d. tag-sanity gate: COUNT under TAG SID must equal R0b ---
SET ORDER TO TAG SID
COUNT
SELECT 1

* ============================================================
* R1. REL declaration + scan-limit honesty
* ============================================================
ECHO === R1a. scan limit as found (expect the 500000 default) ===
REL SCANLIMIT
ECHO === R1b. declare the relation: STUDENTS -> ENROLL ON SID ===
REL ADD STUDENTS ENROLL ON SID
* FIRST-RUN LESSON (2026-09-20): REL LIST's "matches: N" is scoped to the
* CURRENT PARENT record, not the whole relation -- and REL's matcher walks the
* child LINEARLY (that is why SCANLIMIT exists). The canary parent (recno 1,
* SID 50000000) has exactly 8 enrollments, so I3 is a CANARY-SCOPED identity:
* REL LIST 8 == REL ENUM 8 rows == SQLsel canary-join COUNT 8 (R3c).
ECHO === R1c. REL LIST ALL at the DEFAULT budget: the bounds warning MUST fire ===
GO TOP
REL LIST ALL
ECHO === R1d. raise the budget above the child (12M) and re-list ===
REL SCANLIMIT 12000000
ECHO --- R1e. IDENTITY I3 leg 1: canary matches must be exactly 8 ---
REL LIST ALL

* ============================================================
* R2. REL ENUM / REL JOIN emission (bounded -- ENUM prints every tuple)
* ============================================================
ECHO === R2a. REL ENUM for the canary parent: IDENTITY I3 leg 2, exactly 8 rows ===
ECHO --- (current-parent scope; ELAPSED times one full linear child hop) ---
REL ENUM ALL LIMIT 100000 TUPLE STUDENTS.SID, ENROLL.CLS_ID
ECHO === R2b. REL ENUM DISTINCT over parent MAJOR (bounded) ===
REL ENUM DISTINCT LIMIT 50 TUPLE STUDENTS.MAJOR
ECHO === R2c. REL JOIN for the current parent (canary student, 10 rows) ===
GO TOP
REL JOIN ONE LIMIT 10 TUPLE STUDENTS.SID, STUDENTS.LNAME, ENROLL.CLS_ID

* ============================================================
* R3. SQLsel joins at full scale -- counts, not row floods
*     READ THE ACCESS-PATH REPORT: the equi-join on SID with the child tag
*     active must report CDX seek or an honest hybrid, and the report is a
*     datum in its own right (equal row sets do not prove the path).
* ============================================================
ECHO === R3a. IDENTITY I2: INNER JOIN count must equal 5501358 ===
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS S INNER JOIN ENROLL E ON S.SID = E.SID
ECHO === R3b. IDENTITY I4: LEFT JOIN count = I2 + reported left-extended rows ===
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS S LEFT JOIN ENROLL E ON S.SID = E.SID
* MEASURED 2026-09-20: this probe costs ~33 MINUTES, and that cost is itself
* the datum. The access path reports probes=1000000, candidates=5501358 --
* identical to the unfiltered R3a join -- because SQLsel has NO PREDICATE
* PUSHDOWN: WHERE S.SID = 50000000 does not prune the outer scan; the full
* 5.5M-row join runs and is then filtered to 8. The ~0.35 ms/joined-row WHERE
* tax over 5.5M rows is the runtime. The charter never promised an optimizer
* (see the capability boundary in docs/manuals/user/sqlsel.md); this line is
* the number a future optimizer slice gets measured against. The 8 itself
* closes identity I3 (REL LIST 8 == REL ENUM 8 == SQLsel 8).
ECHO === R3c. IDENTITY I3 leg 3: SQLsel canary join must count exactly 8 ===
ECHO --- (multi-minute BY DESIGN: no pushdown -- full join, then filter) ---
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS S INNER JOIN ENROLL E ON S.SID = E.SID WHERE S.SID = 50000000

* ============================================================
* R4. Aggregates: native vs SQLsel on the same predicate, then GROUP BY
* ============================================================
ECHO === R4a. IDENTITY I5 left side: native COUNT FOR MAJOR = "CSCI" ===
COUNT FOR MAJOR = "CSCI"
ECHO === R4b. IDENTITY I5 right side: SQLsel count of the same predicate ===
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS WHERE ALLTRIM(MAJOR) = 'CSCI'
ECHO === R4c. GROUP BY MAJOR over 1M (R28: blank counts are REPORTED, read them) ===
SQLSEL SELECT MAJOR,COUNT(*) AS N,AVG(GPA) AS G FROM STUDENTS GROUP BY MAJOR ORDER BY MAJOR
ECHO === R4d. IDENTITY I6 partner: DISTINCT MAJOR row count == R4c row count ===
SQLSEL SELECT DISTINCT MAJOR FROM STUDENTS ORDER BY MAJOR

* ============================================================
* R5. Subqueries at scale
* ============================================================
* MEASURED 2026-09-20, then READ IN SOURCE (sqlsel_statement.cpp):
*   :1744-1749  WAS a LINEAR SCAN of the materialized vector -- the cache
*               (:1509) made the subquery run ONCE, but every outer probe
*               walked it to first hit. Full-scale (1M outer x 5.5M vector)
*               is ~2.75e12 compares: the 2026-09-20 run sat 68+ minutes with
*               hours to go and was aborted. FIXED 2026-09-21 (findings 3+7
*               repair): uncorrelated IN probes a hash set built once at
*               materialization (in_probe_key preserves value_equal semantics
*               including the numeric-literal rule), and cache hits hand out
*               POINTERS instead of deep-copying the result per outer row.
*               MEASURED post-fix (build Sep 21 2026 15:02:47): R5a 1084 s,
*               R5c full-scale 564 s COUNT = 1000000 -- the probes vanished
*               from the bill; what remains is the one-time materialization
*               at the PERF-1 per-row rate (AIF-168 territory).
*   :1626       a CORRELATED subquery RE-MATERIALIZES its entire inner table
*               on EVERY outer evaluation. The original R5b (1000 outer x
*               5.5M-row materialization each) was a run-killer and never
*               completed a single evaluation batch; 10 outer rows price the
*               re-materialization honestly (~10 x 1M rows).
* GRAMMAR CORRECTION (measured 2026-09-20 tail run, finding 5): a subquery
* predicate must be the ENTIRE WHERE -- 'X AND col IN (...)' and 'X AND
* EXISTS (...)' are both REFUSED (the second falls through to the scalar
* path). So R5a is the PURE IN form, bounded inside the subquery only.
* Expect 1000: only band SIDs are in the list. Cost model post-fix: the
* subquery scan (5.5M x ~200us for the WHERE-carrying inner) IS the price;
* 1M outer probes are O(1) hash lookups. MEASURED 2026-09-21: 1084.2 s.
ECHO === R5a. pure IN, subquery bounded to the canary band: expect 1000 ===
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS S WHERE S.SID IN (SELECT E.SID FROM ENROLL E WHERE E.SID < 50001000)
* R5b (correlated EXISTS at scale) is REMOVED, not bounded: the per-evaluation
* price was MEASURED at ~2349 s (one 5.5M correlated materialization, :1626,
* 427us/row) -- 39 minutes PER OUTER ROW, and the grammar refuses AND-bounding
* of the outer scan. Correlated-at-scale returns to this battery only after
* the :1626 re-materialization fix; until then the OQ-12 mechanism datum
* (evaluation counts) lives in REGRESSION SQLSEL_SUBQUERIES at small scale,
* and the scale price is on record in the benchmarks ledger (PIN-REL3A-013).
ECHO === R5b. correlated-at-scale: SKIPPED BY DESIGN, see comment (39 min/row) ===
* R5c. IDENTITY I7 -- full-scale IN, the findings 3+7 regression proof.
* Unfinishable pre-fix (aborted >7.2 h, 2026-09-20); MEASURED post-fix at
* 564.1 s (2026-09-21, console; promote by this battery's teed rerun).
* FASTER than bounded R5a because the inner scan carries no WHERE: no
* per-row predicate evaluation, ~100us/row instead of ~200us. Expect
* COUNT = 1000000 EXACT (every student enrolled, closed universe) and
* 'correlated=0, uncorrelated=1' in the evaluation-count report.
ECHO === R5c. IDENTITY I7: full-scale IN, expect 1000000 (findings 3+7 regression) ===
SQLSEL SELECT COUNT(*) FROM STUDENTS S WHERE S.SID IN (SELECT E.SID FROM ENROLL E)

* ============================================================
* R6. Set operations -- exact small identities (overlapping 100-row bands)
*     band A: SID < 50000100 (100 rows)  band B: 50000050 <= SID < 50000150
* ============================================================
ECHO === R6a. IDENTITY I8: UNION must produce exactly 150 rows ===
SQLSEL SELECT SID FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID < 50000100 UNION SELECT SID FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50000050 AND SID < 50000150
ECHO === R6b. IDENTITY I8: INTERSECT must produce exactly 50 rows ===
SQLSEL SELECT SID FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID < 50000100 INTERSECT SELECT SID FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50000050 AND SID < 50000150
ECHO === R6c. IDENTITY I8: EXCEPT must produce exactly 50 rows ===
SQLSEL SELECT SID FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID < 50000100 EXCEPT SELECT SID FROM STUDENTS WHERE SID >= 50000050 AND SID < 50000150

* ============================================================
* R7. Restore session state (fixtures were never written)
* ============================================================
ECHO === R7. cleanup: clear relations, restore the 500000 scan limit, close ===
REL CLEAR ALL
REL SCANLIMIT 500000
SELECT 2
CLOSE
SELECT 1
CLOSE

ECHO ============================================================
ECHO RELATIONAL READ-ONLY SHAKEDOWN COMPLETE. Confirm and record:
ECHO   R0a/R0b: PHYSICAL counts 1000000 / 5501358 (I1 anchors).
ECHO   R0c/R0d: COUNT under the active tag EQUALS the physical count
ECHO            beside it. A mismatch means a gutted tag attached
ECHO            silently -- BUILDLMDB HUGE CLEAN YES per table, rerun.
ECHO   R1c: bounds warning FIRED at the 500000 default (honesty datum).
ECHO   I3 : canary triple agreement -- REL LIST 8 == REL ENUM 8 rows ==
ECHO        SQLsel canary join 8 (R1e / R2a / R3c).
ECHO   R3a: INNER JOIN COUNT = 5501358 (I2) -- record ELAPSED + ACCESS PATH.
ECHO   R3b: LEFT COUNT - INNER COUNT = reported left-extended rows (I4).
ECHO   R4a = R4b (I5); R4c row count = R4d row count (I6).
ECHO   R5a: pure-IN count = 1000 exactly (band membership; I7 bounded form).
ECHO   R5b: skipped by design -- correlated is 39 min/row until :1626 is fixed.
ECHO   R5c: full-scale IN = 1000000 EXACT (I7 proper; findings 3+7 regression).
ECHO   R6 : UNION 150, INTERSECT 50, EXCEPT 50 (I8), exact.
ECHO ============================================================
